{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/robokit\/imagetrackermodule"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"RoboKit"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Image Tracker","images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"ImageTrackerModuleCard.png"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Image Tracker module provides functionality for detecting and tracking images in the physical environment using ARKit and visionOS."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/ImageTrackerModule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This module leverages ARKit to track one or more reference images added to an AR Resource Group in your asset catalog. It exposes two main properties: "},{"code":"rootTransform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which represents the calculated center of all tracked images, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackedImagesTransform"},{"text":", which represents the positions of each individual image.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Setup","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Setup"},{"anchor":"Configure-Permissions","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Configure Permissions"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the following key to your app’s Info.plist file:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["<key>NSWorldSensingUsageDescription<\/key>","<string>This app requires world sensing capabilities to track reference images.<\/string>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"xml"},{"level":3,"text":"Create AR Reference Image Group","type":"heading","anchor":"Create-AR-Reference-Image-Group"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open Xcode and go to your asset catalog."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"AR Resource Group","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (e.g., “AR Resources”).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add your tracking images and set their ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"physical size"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" correctly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Define Tracking Images in Code","anchor":"Define-Tracking-Images-in-Code","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each image should be described using its name and a root offset from the reference point in RealityKit coordinates:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import RoboKit","","let trackingImages: [TrackingImage] = [","    TrackingImage(imageName: \"TrackingImage-1\", rootOffset: .init(x: -0.1135, y: 0, z: 0.175)),","    TrackingImage(imageName: \"TrackingImage-2\", rootOffset: .init(x: 0.1135, y: 0, z: -0.175))","]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"RealityKit-Coordinate-System.png","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracking image quality is critical. Avoid compressed images, images with too few or too many geometric features, or with repeating patterns."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensure all tracking images share the same physical orientation.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If using multiple images, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rootOffset"},{"text":" values are used to calculate the center. If using one image, set its offset to ","type":"text"},{"code":".zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Initialize-Image-Tracker","text":"Initialize Image Tracker"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Initialize the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/ImageTracker","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" by providing the resource group name and your array of tracking images:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@State private var imageTracker: RoboKit.ImageTracker = .init(","    arResourceGroupName: \"AR Resources\",","    images: trackingImages",")"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Usage","anchor":"Usage"},{"anchor":"Root-Transform","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Root Transform"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Represents the central position between all tracked images."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".onChange(of: imageTracker.rootTransform) {","    print(imageTracker.rootTransform)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Tracked-Images-Transform","type":"heading","text":"Tracked Images Transform"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Represents the positions of each tracked image:"}]},{"code":[".onChange(of: imageTracker.trackedImagesTransform) {","    print(imageTracker.trackedImagesTransform)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These values update approximately once per second."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"Warning","style":"warning","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Image tracking is not supported in the simulator."}]}]},{"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On visionOS, only one image can be tracked at a time, even if more are visible.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"RealityKit-Coordinate-System.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/robokit.RoboKit\/RealityKit-Coordinate-System.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"identifier":"RealityKit-Coordinate-System.png","type":"image","alt":"RealityKit coordinate system"},"doc://robokit.RoboKit/documentation/RoboKit":{"kind":"symbol","title":"RoboKit","url":"\/documentation\/robokit","role":"collection","images":[{"identifier":"RoboKitLogo.png","type":"icon"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"RoboKit is a framework designed to facilitate the integration between visionOS applications and robotics software."}]},"RoboKitLogo.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/robokit.RoboKit\/RoboKitLogo.png","traits":["1x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/robokit.RoboKit\/RoboKitLogo~dark.png","traits":["1x","dark"]}],"identifier":"RoboKitLogo.png","type":"image","alt":"RoboKit logo."},"ImageTrackerModuleCard.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/robokit.RoboKit\/ImageTrackerModuleCard.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"type":"image","identifier":"ImageTrackerModuleCard.png","alt":null},"doc://robokit.RoboKit/documentation/RoboKit/ImageTracker":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImageTracker","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ImageTracker","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Image Tracker module provides functionality for detecting and tracking images"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the physical environment using ARKit and visionOS."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A class responsible for tracking images using ARKit and providing corresponding transformation data."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"It handles the initialization of AR sessions, image tracking, and updates for tracked anchors.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImageTracker","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/Image